From 3b597f52f6da23d1621e04d9ca4cf9bdb4a297f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafael Palomar <rafael.palomar@ous-research.no>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:22:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] COMP: Install the generated export headers in development
 installs

Slicer 5.12 removed the checked-in per-library export headers
(vtkMRMLExport.h and friends) in favour of GenerateExportHeader output
in the build tree, but never taught the development install(FILES)
lines about them:

- In seven libraries (Base/CLI, Base/Logic, Libs/MRML/{CLI,IDImageIO,
  Logic}, Libs/RemoteIO, Libs/vtkTeem) the old configured header is
  gone too, leaving ${configure_header_file} unset -- the install item
  degenerates to the bare binary dir and configure fails with 'install
  FILES given directory'.  Replace the item with the generated export
  header.
- In four more (Libs/MRML/Core, Libs/MRML/DisplayableManager,
  Libs/vtkITK, Libs/vtkSegmentationCore) the configured header install
  still works, but the generated export header is simply never
  installed.  Append it.

Without this every consumer of the installed development tree fails
with '<lib>Export.h: No such file or directory' (the checked-in
headers used to ride along the ${headers} glob).  Only visible with
*_INSTALL_NO_DEVELOPMENT=OFF as in the standalone Guix build.
---
